# One identity for this org's commits, without rewriting history.
#
# Commits here were made from machines whose git identity had never been set, so
# they carry a hostname-derived address (`user@some-mac.local`, or a Tailscale
# name) that resolves nowhere and links to no account. A few carry a personal or
# GitHub noreply address instead. Correcting that in the commits themselves would
# change every SHA and break every existing clone, fork and permalink, so it is
# corrected for display here: `git log`, `git shortlog` and most tooling read
# this file, and the objects are untouched.
#
# Only identities confirmed to be the same person are listed. Other contributors
# keep their own, whatever shape it is in.

